  "query_preview": "..\nThursday: A cold front will be making its way across the Inland \nNW today. The front is near the Cascades this morning, backed by a\ndeep upper trough. There is some moisture ahead of the front, \ncontributing to PWATs near 125-140% of normal. However most of \nthat is above 150kft or about 500 mb). So the front is forecast to\npass largely dry. Some of the 90 percentile solutions show some \nreturns developing, but that means there is only a 10% chance \nof occurrence. The front moves across the area between late \nmorning to early afternoon, a bit later perhaps near the ID \nPanhandle. Much drier air comes in behind it, along with cooler \ntemperatures. It also comes with wind, around 10-25 mph, with \ngusts of 20-35 mph. The higher range of these will be over \ncentral WA, especially the Okanogan Valley into the Waterville \nPlateau. Red Flag Warnings are in place here from noon to 8 pm \ntoday. Winds abate this evening after about 7 to 9 pm and skies \nclear out. Highs today will be in the 80s, about 10 degrees \ncooler than yesterday.\n\nFriday to Sunday: The Inland NW remains under trough and \nshortwave will be pivoting around it. Friday will remain a bit \nbreezy, but generally dry as relatively weak upper wave rounds \nthrough. A deeper and cooler system swings in Saturday into \nSunday. This will bring shower chances around the northern WA and \nID Panhandle mountains Saturday, possibly SE WA too. Embedded \nt-storms will be possible. The potential for much rain is not \nhigh, with most models not indicating a wetting rain. By Sunday \nthe main chances linger over the ID Panhandle, but PoPs are \nlargely 20% or less. It will be breezy Saturday again, with gusts \nof 15-25 mph. Winds look lighter Sunday but some gusts toward 15 \nmph are possible. Highs will be in the 70s to mid-80s Friday, \ncooling to the 70s on the weekend. Overnight lows may dip into the\n40s and upper 30s Sunday. We may need to monitor for frost in \nsome sheltered valleys. A risk for fog will be found over the \nnorthern valleys Saturday night/early Sunday where low level \nmoisture and light winds will combine.\n\nMonday to Wednesday: Monday dries out then another system moves \nin Tuesday and Wednesday. Limited mountain shower chance come \nTuesday, along with gusty winds. Wednesday will see a broader risk\nand it could actually produce measurable precipitaiton. \nTemperatures moderate to the 70s to mid-80s Monday and Tuesday, \ncooling to the 70s Wednesday. /Solveig",
